# The embedding worker command, as run ON the remote host.
#
# Copy this file to active-embed-remote-cmd.conf and fill in the path for your
# deployment. That file is untracked on purpose: it is the remote account's
# directory layout, which belongs to the host and not to the project. The code
# ships no default -- one would be somebody's private filesystem presented as a
# convenience, and correct on exactly one machine.
#
# Read together with active-embed-remote.conf, which names the ssh destination:
#
#   destination set, command set    -> indexing embeds on the remote host
#   destination set, command unset  -> indexing FAILS, naming this file
#   destination unset               -> indexing embeds locally, which is a
#                                      valid deployment rather than a fallback
#
# A configured remote embedder is never silently replaced by local compute:
# the two produce different vectors, and a collection filled from both is
# wrong in a way no later query reports.
#
# SPEAR_EMBED_REMOTE_CMD in the environment takes precedence over this file.
# An explicitly empty variable means "unset", not "use the file".
#
# One command line. Arguments are split as a shell would split them, so a path
# containing a space is quoted here; a leading ~/ is expanded in the remote
# account. Nothing else is interpreted remotely -- every word is quoted before
# it reaches the far shell.
#
# /srv/inference/embed/venv/bin/python /srv/inference/embed/worker.py
